<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sierra Maestra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sierra Maestra is the highest mountain range of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, in the south-east of the island, rising to Pico Turquino at about 1,970 metres. Its rugged forests sheltered rebels in the wars of independence and, from December 1956, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrillas</a>, who built there the army that overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulgencio-batista">Fulgencio Batista</a> in 1959. Much of it is now protected as a national park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sierra-maestra.jpg" alt="Sierra Maestra" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dr. Anthony R. Picciolo, NOAA NODC · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pico_Torquino_in_the_Sierra_Maestra,_Cuba%27s_highest_mountain,_1974_meters.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
